{
  "title": "Add non-food shopping list categories (Household, Personal Care, \
Pet)",
  "description": "The prod shopping-list corpus \
(data/shopping-list-categories.json) contains hand-typed non-recipe store \
items that have no sensible home in the current food-oriented 16-category \
taxonomy and are labeled 'Other': dish soap, 'Palmolive ultra strength', \
dishwasher detergent, Cascade Platinum (Household/Cleaning); Ibuprofen \
(Personal Care/Pharmacy); dog treats (Pet). After the \
expand-ingredient-categorizer-keywords pass these are the bulk of what's left \
in 'Other' (8 distinct items).\n\
\n\
Adding categories means touching the hardcoded category lists in \
ramekin-core/src/ingredient_categorizer.rs (CATEGORIES), \
ramekin-ui/src/pages/ShoppingListPage.tsx, and \
ramekin-ios/Ramekin/ShoppingListView.swift — see \
p3-shopping-list-category-order-from-api, which would reduce that to one place \
and is worth doing first (not a hard blocker, just ordering).\n\
\n\
When adding the categories, also add starter keywords to data/ingredients.json \
(soap, detergent, paper towel, toilet paper, trash bag, ibuprofen, tylenol, \
advil, toothpaste, shampoo, dog food, dog treat, cat food, cat litter, etc.) \
and update the expected labels for those items in \
data/shopping-list-categories.json, then tighten the MAX_OTHER bounds in \
ramekin-core/tests/shopping_list_categorizer_tests.rs.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "task",
  "labels": [
    "shopping-list",
    "categorizer",
    "web",
    "ios",
  ],
